  <p v-if="rating.differsFromProjection" class="rating-difference">The agents’ average one-year view differs from the central scenario. Their downside assumptions remain part of the research.</p>
  <details><summary>How this rating is calculated</summary><template v-if="rating.independentRecommendations"><p>The bars count each investor’s own recommendation. Each investor independently chooses conditional one-year earnings growth and an exit P/E using the saved source facts. Its target is calculated from compatible reported annual EPS, rather than copied from the shared projection.</p><p>Recommendations reflect conviction and downside risk as well as the conditional target. Buy and sell directions must agree with that investor’s own target; strength is its judgment, not a fixed return band. The gauge averages recommendation strength from Strong sell (−2) through Hold (0) to Strong buy (+2); ties lean toward Hold. Agreement is not forced, and no vote split is prescribed.</p></template><template v-else><p>This earlier assessment rates average saved one-year price views. The bars count individual views using return bands: at least 10% upside for Strong buy and 2% for Buy, with equivalent downside bands.</p><p v-if="rating.mode==='investors'">These older investor views use conditional mixtures of the saved low, central and high scenarios.</p><p v-else>These are the saved supporting and opposing annual researchers’ targets; the virtual investors’ original trading decisions remain in discussion.</p></template><p>Future growth and multiples remain assumptions. These are simulated outlooks, not calibrated probabilities, external analyst recommendations or guaranteed returns. Virtual order limits do not determine the rating.</p></details>
